<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <meta name="color-scheme" content="light dark">
  <meta name="description" content="Privacy Policy for Hidden Player by NINANO Inc. Learn about local settings, YouTube, Apple purchases, and support contact information.">
  <title>Hidden Player — Privacy Policy</title>
  <link rel="icon" type="image/png" href="app-icon.png">
  <style>
    :root { color-scheme: light dark; --bg: #f5f7fc; --card: #fff; --ink: #162338; --muted: #52617a; --line: #dce3ef; --accent: #0754cb; --soft: #eaf2ff; }
    * { box-sizing: border-box; }
    html { scroll-behavior: smooth; scroll-padding-top: 24px; }
    body { margin: 0; background: var(--bg); color: var(--ink); font: 16px/1.65 -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI", sans-serif; }
    a { color: var(--accent); text-underline-offset: 4px; }
    a:hover { text-decoration-thickness: 2px; }
    a:focus-visible, summary:focus-visible { outline: 3px solid var(--accent); outline-offset: 5px; border-radius: 4px; }
    .skip { position: absolute; top: -80px; left: 16px; padding: 10px; background: var(--card); z-index: 2; }
    .skip:focus { top: 12px; }
    .wrap { max-width: 940px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 0 28px; }
    header { display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; gap: 24px; padding: 30px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
    .brand { color: var(--ink); font-size: 17px; font-weight: 700; text-decoration: none; }
    nav { display: flex; gap: 22px; font-size: 14px; }
    nav a { color: var(--muted); text-decoration: none; }
    .hero { padding: 62px 0 46px; display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 144px; align-items: center; gap: 36px; }
    .eyebrow { margin: 0 0 12px; color: var(--accent); font-size: 12px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: .13em; text-transform: uppercase; }
    h1 { margin: 0 0 16px; font-size: clamp(36px, 6vw, 54px); line-height: 1.08; letter-spacing: -.045em; }
    .lead { margin: 0; color: var(--muted); font-size: 18px; max-width: 570px; }
    .app-icon { width: 144px; height: 144px; border-radius: 30px; box-shadow: 0 16px 38px #001a5230; }
    .chips { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 8px; margin-top: 22px; }
    .chip { font-size: 12px; color: var(--muted); padding: 4px 11px; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 100px; }
    section { margin-bottom: 26px; }
    .card { padding: 28px 30px; background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 18px; }
    h2 { margin: 0 0 15px; font-size: 22px; line-height: 1.3; letter-spacing: -.025em; }
    h3 { margin: 0 0 8px; font-size: 16px; }
    p { margin: 0 0 14px; }
    p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
    ol, ul { margin: 0; padding-left: 23px; }
    li + li { margin-top: 9px; }
    .muted { color: var(--muted); }
    .grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 16px; }
    .feature { background: var(--soft); border-radius: 12px; padding: 20px; }
    .feature p { color: var(--muted); font-size: 14px; }
    .range { display: block; color: var(--accent); font-size: 28px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: -.04em; margin-bottom: 5px; }
    .note { margin-top: 18px; font-size: 14px; color: var(--muted); }
    details { padding: 17px 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
    details:last-child { padding-bottom: 0; }
    summary { cursor: pointer; font-weight: 600; padding-right: 8px; }
    details p { padding-top: 12px; color: var(--muted); font-size: 15px; }
    .contact-details { border-left: 3px solid var(--accent); padding-left: 18px; margin: 20px 0; }
    footer { padding: 16px 0 38px; color: var(--muted); font-size: 12px; }
    footer p + p { margin-top: 8px; }
    @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
      :root { --bg: #0b1220; --card: #121d2e; --ink: #edf3ff; --muted: #a8b8d0; --line: #2a3950; --accent: #86baff; --soft: #182a43; }
    }
    @media (max-width: 560px) {
      .wrap { padding: 0 20px; }
      header { gap: 16px; padding: 22px 0; }
      nav { gap: 14px; font-size: 13px; }
      .hero { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 22px; padding: 36px 0 30px; }
      .app-icon { grid-row: 1; width: 76px; height: 76px; border-radius: 17px; }
      .card { padding: 23px 20px; }
      .grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    }
    @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) { html { scroll-behavior: auto; } }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <a class="skip" href="#main">Skip to content</a>
  <div class="wrap">
    <header>
      <a class="brand" href="./">Hidden Player</a>
      <nav aria-label="Page navigation"><a href="./">Support</a><a href="#contact">Contact</a></nav>
    </header>
    <main id="main">
      <div class="hero" style="grid-template-columns: 1fr;">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">NINANO Inc.</p>
          <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
          <p class="lead">Hidden Player is designed to work without a developer-operated account or a personal data collection server.</p>
          <p class="note">Effective date: November 3, 2026</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <section class="card" aria-labelledby="overview-title">
        <h2 id="overview-title">1. Overview</h2>
        <p>This policy describes how NINANO Inc. handles information in connection with Hidden Player for macOS and this support website.</p>
        <p>We do not operate an app account system, collect your viewing or search history on our servers, or include our own advertising, analytics, or tracking SDKs. We do not sell your personal information.</p>
        <p>Hidden Player displays YouTube web content and uses Apple’s in-app purchase services. Those services may process information directly under their own policies, as described below. This policy does not mean that no information is processed by these third parties.</p>
      </section>
      <section class="card" aria-labelledby="local-title">
        <h2 id="local-title">2. Information on your Mac</h2>
        <p>The app stores appearance preferences locally using macOS preferences. Opacity settings are used in memory while the app is running.</p>
        <p>Web content uses WebKit’s standard website data store. Cookies, cache, and other website data may be stored on your Mac, including data that supports YouTube preferences or a website sign-in session. NINANO Inc. does not upload this website data or your sign-in credentials to a developer-operated server.</p>
        <p>Local data is managed by macOS and WebKit. Removing the app does not necessarily remove all stored preferences or website data. Contact us if you need help managing the app’s local data.</p>
      </section>
      <section class="card" aria-labelledby="youtube-title">
        <h2 id="youtube-title">3. YouTube and Google</h2>
        <p>Searches and video requests are sent directly to YouTube and Google. When YouTube pages or embedded players load, Google may receive your IP address, browser or device information, cookies, search terms, and information about playback and interactions. Embedded players may transmit information when they load, even before you interact with the player.</p>
        <p>Google processes this information for purposes described in its policies, which may include providing content, determining playback availability, security, measurement, personalization, and advertising. If you sign in to YouTube, information may be associated with your Google account.</p>
        <p>Use of YouTube content is subject to the <a href="https://www.youtube.com/t/terms">YouTube Terms of Service</a> and <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Google Privacy Policy</a>. You can manage applicable account privacy settings through <a href="https://myaccount.google.com/data-and-privacy">Google Account settings</a>.</p>
      </section>
      <section class="card" aria-labelledby="apple-title">
        <h2 id="apple-title">4. Purchases through Apple</h2>
        <p>Apple processes in-app purchases and payment information. Hidden Player uses StoreKit to receive and verify transaction and entitlement information so it can unlock paid features, restore purchases, and respond to refunds or revoked access.</p>
        <p>NINANO Inc. does not receive your payment card details or Apple Account password. We do not send the app’s StoreKit transaction information to our own server. Apple may separately provide developer sales and financial reports under its services.</p>
        <p>Apple handles information under its <a href="https://www.apple.com/legal/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a> and <a href="https://www.apple.com/legal/privacy/data/en/app-store/">App Store privacy information</a>.</p>
      </section>
      <section class="card" aria-labelledby="support-title">
        <h2 id="support-title">5. Support emails</h2>
        <p>If you email us, we receive your email address, the contents of your message, and any attachments you choose to send. We use that information to respond to your request and resolve the issue. Email is handled through Gmail and may also be processed by your email provider.</p>
        <p>We retain support correspondence only as long as reasonably needed to handle your request, maintain necessary support records, or meet applicable legal obligations. To request deletion of information you sent us, contact the address below. Please do not send passwords or payment card details.</p>
      </section>
      <section class="card" aria-labelledby="website-title">
        <h2 id="website-title">6. This support website</h2>
        <p>This website is hosted on GitHub Pages. We do not add analytics scripts, tracking pixels, advertising scripts, or contact forms. GitHub may process technical information, such as your IP address and request logs, to provide and secure its hosting service.</p>
        <p>See the <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement">GitHub General Privacy Statement</a> for information about its practices.</p>
      </section>
      <section class="card" aria-labelledby="choices-title">
        <h2 id="choices-title">7. Your choices</h2>
        <p>You can stop using the app, manage your Google and Apple account settings, and choose what information to include when contacting support. Requests about information held directly by Google, Apple, or GitHub should be directed to the relevant provider.</p>
        <p>Depending on your location, you may have rights concerning your personal information, including access, correction, or deletion. For information held by NINANO Inc. through support correspondence, contact us below.</p>
      </section>
      <section class="card" aria-labelledby="changes-title">
        <h2 id="changes-title">8. Changes to this policy</h2>
        <p>We may update this policy when the app or our information practices change. The effective date at the top identifies the current version. If our practices materially change, we will provide notice as required.</p>
      </section>
      <section class="card" id="contact" aria-labelledby="contact-title">
        <h2 id="contact-title">9. Contact</h2>
        <p><strong>NINANO Inc.</strong><br>Email: <a href="mailto:ninano0916@gmail.com">ninano0916@gmail.com</a></p>
        <p class="note">For questions about this policy or privacy requests related to Hidden Player, please contact us at this address.</p>
      </section>
    </main>
    <footer>
      <p>© 2026 NINANO Inc. All rights reserved.</p>
      <p><a href="./">Support</a> · <a href="privacy.html" aria-current="page">Privacy Policy</a></p>
    </footer>
  </div>
</body>
</html>
